          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رعد و برق (ra'd-o barq) — \"a thunderstorm; thunder and lightning\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دیشب رعد و برق شدیدی بود. Dishab ra'd-o barq-e shadidi bud. Last night there was a heavy thunderstorm."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ra'd 'thunder' + o 'and' + barq 'lightning'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ra'd-o barq joins two Arabic loans with Persian o 'and': ra'd from Arabic raʿd 'thunder' and barq from Arabic barq 'flashing, lightning' (EtymDB lists both)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
